  "observations": [
    "Opened each final640/331/342PNG separately at original detail. Each shows two separate slashed open AC terminals on the left, with the sole AC mark between them.",
    "The upper wire rises, runs across the top and descends to one filled downward contact meeting the upper outline of the straight bonded strip. The strip visibly extends left of the contact; the contact was not moved to its geometric leftmost tip.",
    "The two layers share one horizontal interface. The upper layer is plain and the lower layer diagonally hatched; no Cu/Fe identity, coefficient ordering, bent alternative or extra state appears.",
    "The right strip connection continues right, down and left into the heater's right port. The heater's left port returns to the lower AC terminal. There is one series route and no parallel heater branch or invented support wall.",
    "Heater is the only English equipment label and remains wholly within its rectangle at640/331/342. The AC mark, contact, interface and hatch distinction remain visible at both mobile widths, without text overlap or clipping.",
    "The filled downward tip represents the printed contact, not a current-flow arrow. No current arrows, particle loops, heating animation, numerical calibration or answer-bearing annotation were added. Initial native rendering succeeded without repair."
  ],
